WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Good morning John,

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.840
So I got some good news and I got some bad news about Syria

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.400
That's a lie. I only have bad news, it is only bad news, it is a terrible situation.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.480
But there is no solving problems that you don't understand

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.860
So, here it is, in the next 5 or 6 minutes, we're going to understand Syria...

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.600
At least more than we did before...

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.780
Alright, lets start at the foundation of Syria

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.360
A bunch of Western powers are introducing the idea of Nation States to the rest of the world

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.560
They draw a shape on a piece of paper and say: "This shape shall be Syria"

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.940
Inside that shape, are lots of different sorts of people who have various degrees of historical and social ties.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.240
There are Christians, and Druze, and Sunni Muslim, and Alawites...

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:39.520
And of course, Pluralism does not necessarily breed violence but we... lets.. just.. wait and see.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.820
Fast-Forward to the Cold War:

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.360
The First World of the USA and the Second World of the USSR

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.820
are nabbing up alliances with the "Third World" of...everyone else

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.400
Russia nabbed Syria

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.500
through a combination of diplomacy and giving guns,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.300
they helped the ostensibly Socialist Ba'ath Party, take control in Syria

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.160
The Ba'ath Party was run by Alawites, the leader was a guy who's lats name was Assad.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.280
The father of the current Assad

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.700
And even though the Cold War is now over,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.660
(though apparently no one has told to the United States defence budgets..)

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.680
Russia continues to be closely allied with Syria

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.200
And relies on Syria for it's sweet warm water ports which Russia lacks because it is Russia..

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.880
And here since the Ba'ath took over in 1970, Syria has become kind of a segregated place.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.680
The scholarships go to Alawi children, government contracts go to Alawi businesses,

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.220
There are literally lanes of traffic that only Alawite people are allowed to drive in.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.000
The majority of Syria are Sunni Muslim.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.300
The official Sunni Muslim stands of Alawites is that they have rejected the teachings of Islam..

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.920
So that, combined with the fact that they've been  repressed for like 40 years

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.200
creates some sectarian tension that during the Arab Spring.. broke open.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.800
This is a struggle between a powerful minority and a disenfranchised majority.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.720
Peaceful pro-democracy protests were swiftly punished by the Assad regime.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.120
First, by putting people in jail (then they kept protesting), then they started to kill them.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:04.340
then, they protested more violently, then they started to torture their children and kill their families...

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.600
It's bad...

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.060
Then a big hunk of the army defectors became the Free Syrian Army... Urgh...

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.300
Continues however to get more confusing while the original protests was pro democracy protest

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.300
and there are still many rebels fighting for a democratic future,

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.900
there are now tons of different rebel groups who all want different things,

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.840
and some of them like each other. and some of them don't:

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.600
Some of them love Al-Qaeda and some of them love democracy

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.320
This isn't Star Wars. there is no rebel alliance, it's messy, and it's muddy and to make things worse,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:38.200
if we are talking about Star Wars here, Assad has basically killed Luke Skywalker and Han and Leia

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.120
and blown up Alderaan and Admiral Ackbar's gone to.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.940
Assad forces has killed so many Non-Alawite civilian and military leaders,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.200
that it's completely unclear who the heck would take over if he left

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.060
Now, for years all of this was happening outside of the international spotlight,

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.960
But then - chemical weapons.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.800
President Obama had previously stated there is a "Red Line"

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.260
and that if Syria uses chemical weapons... Something

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.220
And it looks as if Assad's forces did use chemical weapons.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.200
Sarin gas was definitely used, and it was definitely used  on the enemies of Assad's regime.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.300
Now, claims to the contrary to me feel very much like 1960's America

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.880
where white people actually believed that African-American radicals bombed an African-American church

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.900
in order to make the KKK look bad.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.540
Urgh.....

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:26.060
Russia has veto-powered the UN security council and they have never allowed the UN to take action against Assad

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:31.940
because Russia loves Assad, and he's the only ally they have in the Middle East, and those warm water ports...

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.540
Now, Obama wants to enforce his "Red Line" even without the UN support,

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.560
and the American people are like: "Oh God, No, not again, No!!!"

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.900
So the president's like: "Well, once upon a time it was congress'es job to decide whether or not

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:47.460
"we attack other countries, so lets let them decide!" which is funny because as we all know,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:52.260
if congress were on fire congress could not pass the "Pour Water on Congress" act

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.700
Just like Russia needs Assad, Assad needs Russia

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.320
and so, Assad is willing to do a lot of what Russia tells him to do...

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:05.360
which leads us, to John Kerry, making the weirdest possible accidental act of diplomacy of all time

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.540
when he was like: "Yeah, I mean Assad can prevent us from attacking him...

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.180
"By giving us all of his chemical weapons! it's not gonna happen, but he could do it"

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.620
And Russia was like: "Oh! Hey! Ha! Oh! We.. we could do that!"

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.640
This is nice for Russia because now they get to put on the Well-Mannered-Diplomatic-Hero Hat which they

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:24.300
don't get to wear very much lately due to all of their corruption and dismantling of democracy and freedom

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.520
Plus, lets not forget that Russia blocking any possible action by the UN

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.100
is why we are in this mess in the first place

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.420
Now, it's possible that Russia is just enabling Assad's stalling

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.780
And if it happens, it will be extremely complicated to collect a bunch of chemical weapons

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.900
out of a country that Is In the Middle of a Civil War!

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.740
but it would be an excellent outcome to be able to enforce the international norm against chemical weapons,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.760
not have to blowing anything up or ask congress to do anything!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.320
but it comes down to it that anyone who said that they know what we should in this situation

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.860
is either being disingenuous or they don't know what they're talking about.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.860
Maybe attacking Assad and empowering the rebels will save millions of lives,

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.020
maybe it will cost millions of lives.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.060
Maybe the power vacuumed off by Assad will be filled with Islamists who'd be sympathetic to Al-Qaeda.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.080
The problem with the future is that it is unknowable

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.980
and so, we don't really know what we should do

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.500
But there is something that We can do

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.920
Maybe not to the overall geo-politics of the situation but for individual people.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:18.560
The Syrian civil war has displaced over 2 million people

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.080
and if you would like to join me in donating to the UN refuge agency,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.780
that money will go to helping those people rebuild their lives.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.360
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

